== Criterion 1 — the test passes as written ==
cmd: cd bf2-check && go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestGet_CommitNeverFallsBackToVCSRevision' ./internal/version/
out: === RUN   TestGet_CommitNeverFallsBackToVCSRevision
     --- PASS: TestGet_CommitNeverFallsBackToVCSRevision (0.00s)
     ok  budget2/internal/version  0.002s ; NAMED_EXIT=0
The cache is defeated by -count=1; the test exists under that exact name (Read of
bf2-check/internal/version/version_test.go lines 260-292), and it asserts what its name claims:
  Commit = "unknown"                       // the unstamped default
  readBuildInfo -> vcs.revision "deadbeefcafe1234", vcs.modified "true"
  info := Get()
  line 286-288: info.Commit must still be "unknown"    <- the no-fallback contract
  line 289-291: info.VCSRevision must be "deadbeefcafe1234" <- harness-integrity guard
Both the Commit var and readBuildInfo are restored in a single t.Cleanup (lines 266-271).

